  "unit": "relative mag (wing index; 0 = median)",
  "method": "unWISE epoch coadds, background-subtracted median of 1-px rings in the unsaturated PSF wings, ratio to the all-epoch median",
  "notes": [
   "Too bright for normal photometry: the star's core is saturated in WISE and in SPHEREx. 'mag' here is a RELATIVE brightness index (0 = median; positive = fainter) from the unsaturated outer wings of the star image, not a magnitude.",
   "Index from rings 11–17 px (W1) and 13–19 px (W2) around the star in 37 + 37 unWISE epochs (2010–2024).",
   "Period search (100–1000 d) on the index: best period 246 d (W1) and 247 d (W2), matching the known Mira period of 246.12 d (AAVSO VSX).",
   "WISE visits this star only about every 6 months, so an alias period near 713 d fits almost as well; the data are consistent with the known period but could not single it out without it.",
   "Folded on 246.12 d, one sine wave explains 76 % of the W1 index variation (semi-amplitude 0.31 mag in the index).",
   "NEOWISE profile-fit magnitudes of R Dra scatter by up to ~2 mag within single visits (beyond the saturation-correction range) and are not used.",
   "SPHEREx points (synthesized at 3.4/4.6 µm from per-epoch spectra) are not possible: the star is saturated in SPHEREx."
  ],
